#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Makes Navigation's indoor maps from the game's own files: the plan of every building and cave the continents
place, as the game's own indoor minimap draws it, to lay over the world map while the player is inside.

The game keeps an indoor minimap per part (group) of a building (WMO): its client table WMOMinimapTexture names,
per building (its WMO ID, in the root file's header), part and block, one texture. A block is 128 yards of the
part's own floor plan (the building's x and y, as its root file's part list boxes it), 2 texels a yard, from the
part's box minimum: block column BlockX along x, block row BlockY along y. Each texture is the plan seen from
above, x to the right and y upwards (its last row is the block's lowest y); a full block is 256 x 256, a part's
only block (and some last ones) the smallest power of two from 32 that holds the rest. The game's alpha is on or
off (DXT1); where it is off the texture is black.

A part whose blocks do not fit its box (a block missing or too many, a texture of another size), or whose drawn
texels do not lie on its own triangles seen from above (fewer than ON_SHAPE of them within two texels), has
textures made for another shape of the building: it is left out, as is a part the table names that the building
does not have, and one that draws fewer than SPECK texels.

Per part, its blocks are laid into one picture, the game's black under its clear texels replaced by the colour of
the edge near it, its edge softened (the alpha blurred a little, the darkest texels on the edge faded: DXT1 leaves
a black rim) and cut to what is drawn, with two clear texels around. It is then resized, its proportions kept,
into a texture of powers of two: of the sizes that keep at least SHARP of the game's texels a yard (and the sides
at most WIDEST), the smallest, at the largest scale it allows. The picture lies at the texture's top left, the
rest of the texture is clear. Every mipmap is made from the picture itself, in premultiplied alpha with Lanczos,
a clear texel again taking the colour of the edge near it, so the game's filter never blends in black.

  assets/optimized/Navigation/Art/Indoors/<root file>-<part>.blp BLP2, DXT5 with every mipmap (Doc/guides/images.md)

Every placement of a building that has such a picture (the object files' MODF: its place, its turn and its scale;
one tilted more than TILT degrees is left out, its plan would not lie flat), as staging for the set Indoors:

  dev/data/staging/indoors.jsonl    one line per building: key its root file's ID, fields
    groups   per part with a picture: group (its number in the building), file (the picture's name), left, bottom,
             right, top (where the texture's corners lie, in the building's own x and y, yards), low and high (the
             part's height, its box's z), outdoor (true for a part without the game's indoor flag), open (true
             for a part under the sky though the game counts it indoors: a city's street, square or courtyard,
             which the game lights as outdoors, its flag EXTERIOR_LIT, and whose area its table WMOAreaTable
             counts as outdoors, AREA_OUTDOOR; Stormwind and Orgrimmar are each one building)
    placed   per placement: map (the continent's instance), x, y, z (where the building's origin stands, in world
             yards: x grows to the north, y to the west), yaw (the game's turn about the up axis, degrees), scale
    tiles    the terrain tiles its placements' boxes touch (keys of the set Tiles), for the index byTile

A point (bx, by) of the building lies in the world at
    x = X - scale * (bx * cos(yaw) - by * sin(yaw))
    y = Y - scale * (bx * sin(yaw) + by * cos(yaw))
so on a map with north up the picture is turned counterclockwise by yaw - 90 degrees about its building's origin.

The input, as the game stores it:
  game files      a folder with adt-obj0/ (the object files, <tile key>.adt), wmo/ (the root files <file ID>.wmo
                  and their part files <file ID>_<part>.wmo, as for dev/tools/walk-data) and wmo-minimap/ (the
                  indoor minimap textures, <file ID>.blp); its build.txt names the product and version
  client tables   a folder of the game's client tables as CSV (WMOMinimapTexture)
Options: --only <file>[,<file>...] those buildings only (their pictures and staging lines; the others' pictures
stay), --processes N, --check <folder> <minimap textures> pictures to look at (not shipped): the game's outdoor
minimap of some known places (the set Tiles' textures, <file ID>.blp) with the indoor maps laid over, as the
staging places them.

Needs Python with Pillow and NumPy, and ImageMagick 7 (magick).

Usage:  dev/tools/indoor-art <game files> <client tables> [--only files] [--processes N] [--check folder textures]
"""
import csv
import json
import math
import struct
import sys
from importlib.machinery import SourceFileLoader
from importlib.util import module_from_spec, spec_from_loader
from multiprocessing import Pool
from pathlib import Path

import numpy as np
from PIL import Image

ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
OUT = ROOT / "assets" / "optimized" / "Navigation" / "Art" / "Indoors"  # into the addon's Art/ by dev/build
STAGING = ROOT / "dev" / "data" / "staging" / "indoors.jsonl"
GAMES = {"wowf": "forever", "wow_classic_beta": "forever-beta"}  # as dev/tools/data game names them

BLOCK = 128            # yards of a part's plan in one block
TEXELS = 2             # the game's texels a yard
SMALLEST = 32          # the game's smallest texture side
SHARP = 2 ** -0.5      # the least share of the game's texels a picture keeps: half a power of two
WIDEST = 1024          # a texture's longest side (Doc/guides/images.md)
LEAST = 4              # a texture's shortest side: one DXT block
SOFT = 0.6             # the alpha's blur, in the game's texels (a Gaussian's width)
DARK = 32 / 255        # an edge texel darker than this fades towards the game's black
MARGIN = 2             # clear texels around the cut picture
SPECK = 8              # texels: a part that draws fewer (two square yards) draws nothing
ON_SHAPE = 0.9         # the least share of a part's drawn texels on its own triangles
TILT = 10              # degrees: a placement tilted more is left out
GRID = 64              # tiles along each side of a continent
TILE = 1600 / 3        # a tile's side in yards
HALF = GRID / 2 * TILE # yards from a continent's middle to its edges
INDOOR = 0x2000        # a part's flag: indoors
EXTERIOR_LIT = 0x40    # a part's flag: lit as outdoors (by the sky)
AREA_OUTDOOR = 0x4     # a part's area's flag (WMOAreaTable): outdoors

# Places to look at with --check: a name, the continent's instance, the middle (world x and y) and how far around.
CHECKS = [
    ("goldshire", 0, -9445, 30, 75),
    ("northshire-abbey", 0, -8897, -178, 90),
    ("echo-ridge-mine", 0, -8646, -132, 110),
    ("stormwind", 0, -8740, 690, 330),
    ("ironforge", 0, -4880, -1000, 420),
    ("undercity", 0, 1600, 240, 330),
    ("thunder-bluff", 1, -1220, 30, 260),
    ("orgrimmar", 1, 1700, -4400, 650),
]


def module(name, path):
    loader = SourceFileLoader(name, str(path))
    found = module_from_spec(spec_from_loader(name, loader))
    loader.exec_module(found)
    return found


WALK = module("walk_data", ROOT / "dev" / "tools" / "walk-data")  # the placements, and terrain-art's BLP writer
ART = WALK.ART


# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  The game's files
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
def build_of(folder):
    """(game version, build) of a game files' folder, from its build.txt."""
    info = dict(line.split("\t", 1) for line in (folder / "build.txt").read_text(encoding="utf-8").splitlines() if "\t" in line)
    game = GAMES.get(info.get("product"))
    if not game:
        sys.exit(f"{folder}/build.txt names no product SaneUI knows ({info.get('product')})")
    return game, int(info["version"].rsplit(".", 1)[1])


def building(path):
    """A root file's WMO ID and its parts: [(flags, box: min x, y, z, max x, y, z)]."""
    data = path.read_bytes()
    wmo, parts = None, []
    for name, at, size in ART.pieces(data, 0, len(data)):
        if name == b"MOHD":
            wmo = struct.unpack_from("<I", data, at + 32)[0]
        elif name == b"MOGI":
            for start in range(at, at + size, 32):
                flags, *box = struct.unpack_from("<I6f", data, start)
                parts.append((flags, tuple(box)))
    return wmo, parts


def part_id(path):
    """A part file's number in the game's tables (its MOGP's unique ID, WMOAreaTable's WMOGroupID); None without."""
    if not path.exists():
        return None
    data = path.read_bytes()
    for name, at, size in ART.pieces(data, 0, len(data)):
        if name == b"MOGP":
            return struct.unpack_from("<I", data, at + 56)[0]
    return None


def area_flags(tables):
    """{(WMO ID, part's unique ID): its area's flags} of the game's table WMOAreaTable."""
    found = {}
    with open(tables / "WMOAreaTable.csv", encoding="utf-8") as table:
        for row in csv.DictReader(table):
            found[(int(row["WMOID"]), int(row["WMOGroupID"]))] = int(row["Flags"] or 0)
    return found


def textures(tables):
    """{WMO ID: {part: {(block column, block row): texture file ID}}} of the game's table."""
    found = {}
    with open(tables / "WMOMinimapTexture.csv", encoding="utf-8") as table:
        for row in csv.DictReader(table):
            if row["FileDataID"] not in ("", "0"):
                found.setdefault(int(row["WMOID"]), {}).setdefault(int(row["GroupNum"]), {})[
                    (int(row["BlockX"]), int(row["BlockY"]))] = int(row["FileDataID"])
    return found


def side(texels, least=SMALLEST, most=BLOCK * TEXELS):
    """The smallest power of two from least that holds so many texels, at most most."""
    size = least
    while size < texels - 1e-6 and size < most:
        size *= 2
    return size


def blocks_of(box):
    """How many blocks a part's plan has along x and y."""
    return (max(1, math.ceil((box[3] - box[0]) / BLOCK - 1e-6)), max(1, math.ceil((box[4] - box[1]) / BLOCK - 1e-6)))


def fits(box, blocks, sizes):
    """Whether a part's blocks fit its box: every block there, each texture of its size (a full block, or the
    last one's rest)."""
    across, up = blocks_of(box)
    if set(blocks) != {(column, row) for column in range(across) for row in range(up)}:
        return False
    for (column, row), file in blocks.items():
        rest = (side(TEXELS * (box[3] - box[0] - BLOCK * column)), side(TEXELS * (box[4] - box[1] - BLOCK * row)))
        full = BLOCK * TEXELS
        if not all(have in ((full, want) if more else (want,)) for have, want, more in
                   zip(sizes[file], rest, (across > 1, up > 1))):
            return False
    return True


def texture_size(path):
    return struct.unpack_from("<2I", path.read_bytes()[:20], 12)


# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  A part's picture
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
def blur(grid, sigma):
    """A Gaussian blur of sigma texels, along both sides in turn (the edges clear)."""
    reach = max(1, int(math.ceil(sigma * 3)))
    kernel = np.exp(-0.5 * (np.arange(-reach, reach + 1) / sigma) ** 2)
    kernel /= kernel.sum()
    padded = np.pad(grid, reach)
    rows = sum(weight * padded[:, k:k + grid.shape[1]] for k, weight in enumerate(kernel))
    return sum(weight * rows[k:k + grid.shape[0], :] for k, weight in enumerate(kernel))


def smoothstep(low, high, value):
    t = np.clip((value - low) / (high - low), 0, 1)
    return t * t * (3 - 2 * t)


def bleed(rgb, alpha):
    """Colour where the picture is clear: the edge's near it, carried outwards (pulled down to coarser grids,
    pushed back up)."""
    levels, colour, weight = [], rgb * alpha[..., None], alpha
    while True:
        levels.append((colour, weight))
        if colour.shape[0] == 1 and colour.shape[1] == 1:
            break
        high, wide = colour.shape[:2]
        colour = np.pad(colour, ((0, high % 2), (0, wide % 2), (0, 0)))
        weight = np.pad(weight, ((0, high % 2), (0, wide % 2)))
        colour = colour.reshape(colour.shape[0] // 2, 2, colour.shape[1] // 2, 2, 3).sum(axis=(1, 3))
        weight = weight.reshape(weight.shape[0] // 2, 2, weight.shape[1] // 2, 2).sum(axis=(1, 3))
    shown = None
    for colour, weight in reversed(levels):
        own = colour / np.maximum(weight, 1e-6)[..., None]
        if shown is not None:
            up = np.repeat(np.repeat(shown, 2, 0), 2, 1)[:own.shape[0], :own.shape[1]]
            own = np.where((weight > 0)[..., None], own, up)
        shown = own
    return shown


def plan(blocks, folder):
    """A part's blocks laid out as one picture: RGB and alpha (0 to 1), rows from its highest y."""
    across = max(column for column, _ in blocks) + 1
    up = max(row for _, row in blocks) + 1
    full = BLOCK * TEXELS
    picture = np.zeros((up * full, across * full, 4), np.float32)
    for (column, row), file in blocks.items():
        with Image.open(folder / f"{file}.blp") as image:
            texels = np.asarray(image.convert("RGBA"), np.float32) / 255
        high, wide = texels.shape[:2]
        bottom = (up - row) * full  # the block's last row is its lowest y
        picture[bottom - high:bottom, column * full:column * full + wide] = texels
    return picture[..., :3], picture[..., 3]


def softened(rgb, alpha):
    """The alpha with its edge softened: the darkest texels on the edge faded, then blurred a little."""
    solid = alpha > 0.5
    clear = ~solid
    near = np.zeros_like(solid)  # solid texels beside a clear one
    near[1:, :] |= clear[:-1, :]
    near[:-1, :] |= clear[1:, :]
    near[:, 1:] |= clear[:, :-1]
    near[:, :-1] |= clear[:, 1:]
    near &= solid
    alpha = np.where(near, alpha * smoothstep(0, DARK, rgb.max(axis=2)), np.where(solid, alpha, 0))
    return blur(alpha, SOFT)


def scale_of(wide, high):
    """The texture's size and the picture's size in it, (W, H, w, h): of the scales that keep at least SHARP of the
    game's texels (lower only where WIDEST needs it), the one with the smallest texture, and of those the largest."""
    top = min(1.0, WIDEST / wide, WIDEST / high)
    low = min(SHARP, top)
    scales = {top, low}
    for length in (wide, high):
        size = LEAST
        while size <= WIDEST:
            if low <= size / length <= top:
                scales.add(size / length)
            size *= 2
    best = None
    for scale in scales:
        w, h = max(1, math.ceil(scale * wide - 1e-6)), max(1, math.ceil(scale * high - 1e-6))
        width, height = side(w, LEAST, WIDEST), side(h, LEAST, WIDEST)
        if w > width or h > height:
            continue
        pick = (width * height, -scale)
        if best is None or pick < best[0]:
            best = (pick, (width, height, w, h))
    return best[1]


def levels(rgb, alpha, width, height, w, h):
    """Every mipmap of the texture, largest first, as RGBA pictures: each from the cut picture itself (texels
    rgb, alpha), resized in premultiplied alpha with Lanczos into its place at the top left."""
    high, wide = alpha.shape
    # The whole texture in the picture's own texels; what lies past the picture is clear.
    across, down = width * wide / w, height * high / h
    pad = ((0, max(0, math.ceil(down) + 1 - high)), (0, max(0, math.ceil(across) + 1 - wide)))
    planes = [np.pad(rgb[..., k] * alpha, pad) for k in range(3)] + [np.pad(alpha, pad)]
    images = [Image.fromarray(plane.astype(np.float32), "F") for plane in planes]
    out, k = [], 0
    while True:
        size = (max(1, width >> k), max(1, height >> k))
        made = [np.asarray(image.resize(size, Image.Resampling.LANCZOS, box=(0, 0, across, down)), np.float32)
                for image in images]
        a = np.clip(made[3], 0, 1)
        colour = np.stack(made[:3], axis=-1) / np.maximum(a, 1e-6)[..., None]
        colour = bleed(np.clip(colour, 0, 1), np.where(a > 1 / 255, a, 0))
        a = np.where(a >= 250 / 255, 1, a)
        out.append(Image.fromarray((np.dstack([np.clip(colour, 0, 1), a]) * 255).round().astype(np.uint8), "RGBA"))
        if size == (1, 1):
            break
        k += 1
    return out


def blp(pictures):
    """A BLP2 file of RGBA mipmaps, largest first: DXT5 (encoding 2, alpha depth 8, alpha encoding 7)."""
    parts = [ART.dxt5(picture) for picture in pictures]
    offsets, start = [], 148 + 1024  # the header, then a palette DXT does not use
    for part in parts:
        offsets.append(start)
        start += len(part)
    unused = [0] * (16 - len(parts))
    header = b"BLP2" + struct.pack("<I4B2I", 1, 2, 8, 7, 1, pictures[0].width, pictures[0].height)
    header += struct.pack("<16I", *offsets, *unused) + struct.pack("<16I", *(len(part) for part in parts), *unused)
    return header + bytes(1024) + b"".join(parts)


def triangles(path):
    """Every triangle of a part's file in the building's own space: an (n, 3, 3) array of corners (x, y, z)."""
    data = path.read_bytes()
    top = WALK.chunks(data, 0, len(data))
    if b"MOGP" not in top:
        return np.zeros((0, 3, 3))
    at, size = top[b"MOGP"]
    inner = WALK.chunks(data, at + 68, at + size)
    if b"MOVT" not in inner or not (b"MOVI" in inner or b"MOVX" in inner):
        return np.zeros((0, 3, 3))
    vat, vsize = inner[b"MOVT"]
    vertices = np.frombuffer(data, np.float32, vsize // 4, vat).reshape(-1, 3)
    kind, width = (b"MOVI", np.uint16) if b"MOVI" in inner else (b"MOVX", np.uint32)
    iat, isize = inner[kind]
    indices = np.frombuffer(data, width, isize // np.dtype(width).itemsize, iat).astype(np.int64)
    indices = indices[:len(indices) // 3 * 3].reshape(-1, 3)
    return vertices[indices[(indices < len(vertices)).all(axis=1)]]


def on_shape(alpha, box, path):
    """The share of the drawn texels (alpha, rows from the plan's highest y) that lie on the part's own triangles
    seen from above (within two texels): about all of them when the textures were made for this shape."""
    from PIL import ImageDraw
    drawn = alpha > 0.5
    if not drawn.any():
        return 1.0
    high, wide = alpha.shape
    mask = Image.new("1", (wide, high), 0)
    draw = ImageDraw.Draw(mask)
    for corners in triangles(path):
        draw.polygon([((x - box[0]) * TEXELS, high - (y - box[1]) * TEXELS) for x, y, _ in corners], fill=1)
    shape = np.asarray(mask, bool)
    for _ in range(2):
        grown = shape.copy()
        grown[1:, :] |= shape[:-1, :]
        grown[:-1, :] |= shape[1:, :]
        grown[:, 1:] |= shape[:, :-1]
        grown[:, :-1] |= shape[:, 1:]
        shape = grown
    return float((drawn & shape).sum() / drawn.sum())


def picture(job):
    """One part's picture, written; gives (file, part, its rectangle (left, bottom, right, top), its bytes), or
    (file, part, None, why) when it is left out."""
    file, part, box, blocks, folder, shape = job
    rgb, alpha = plan(blocks, folder)
    if (alpha > 0.5).sum() < SPECK:
        return file, part, None, "nothing drawn"
    if not shape.exists():
        return file, part, None, "no part file"
    if on_shape(alpha, box, shape) < ON_SHAPE:
        return file, part, None, "another shape"
    pad = MARGIN + int(math.ceil(SOFT * 3)) + 1  # room for the blur and the margin at the plan's edges
    rgb, alpha = np.pad(rgb, ((pad, pad), (pad, pad), (0, 0))), np.pad(alpha, pad)
    rgb = bleed(rgb, (alpha > 0.5).astype(np.float32))  # the game's black under its clear texels never shows
    alpha = softened(rgb, alpha)
    rows, columns = np.nonzero((alpha > 2 / 255).any(axis=1))[0], np.nonzero((alpha > 2 / 255).any(axis=0))[0]
    r0, r1, c0, c1 = rows[0] - MARGIN, rows[-1] + MARGIN + 1, columns[0] - MARGIN, columns[-1] + MARGIN + 1
    rgb, alpha = rgb[r0:r1, c0:c1], alpha[r0:r1, c0:c1]
    high, wide = alpha.shape
    width, height, w, h = scale_of(wide, high)
    # Where the texture's corners lie in the building's x and y: its top left is the cut's top left.
    plan_high = (max(row for _, row in blocks) + 1) * BLOCK * TEXELS
    left = box[0] + (c0 - pad) / TEXELS
    top = box[1] + (plan_high - (r0 - pad)) / TEXELS
    right = left + width * wide / w / TEXELS
    bottom = top - height * high / h / TEXELS
    data = blp(levels(rgb, alpha, width, height, w, h))
    path = OUT / f"{file}-{part}.blp"
    path.write_bytes(data)
    with Image.open(path) as back:  # read back by Pillow's own BLP reader
        assert back.size == (width, height), f"{path.name} reads back as {back.size}"
    return file, part, (left, bottom, right, top), len(data)


# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  The placements
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
def tilt(turn):
    """How far a placement leans from upright, in degrees (its turns about the two level axes)."""
    lean = math.cos(math.radians(turn[0])) * math.cos(math.radians(turn[2]))
    return math.degrees(math.acos(max(-1.0, min(1.0, lean))))


def tiles_of(continent, box):
    """The keys of the terrain tiles a world box (north, south, west, east) touches."""
    north, south, west, east = box
    rows = range(max(0, int(32 - north / TILE)), min(GRID - 1, int(32 - south / TILE)) + 1)
    columns = range(max(0, int(32 - west / TILE)), min(GRID - 1, int(32 - east / TILE)) + 1)
    return [continent * GRID * GRID + row * GRID + column for row in rows for column in columns]


def placed(where, continent):
    px, py, pz = where["at"]
    return {"map": continent, "x": round(HALF - pz, 2), "y": round(HALF - px, 2), "z": round(py, 2),
            "yaw": round(where["turn"][1] % 360, 2), "scale": round(where["scale"], 4)}


# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Pictures to look at (--check)
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
def check(folder, minimap, lines):
    """For each place of CHECKS: the game's outdoor minimap (2 texels a yard, north up), and beside it the same
    with every indoor map laid over that the staging places there, lowest part first."""
    from PIL import ImageDraw
    found = ART.tiles()
    folder.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    cache = {}
    for name, continent, middle_x, middle_y, reach in CHECKS:
        side_texels = int(2 * reach * TEXELS)
        north, west = middle_x + reach, middle_y + reach
        xs = north - (np.arange(side_texels) + 0.5) / TEXELS   # world x of each row
        ys = west - (np.arange(side_texels) + 0.5) / TEXELS    # world y of each column
        ground = np.zeros((side_texels, side_texels, 3), np.float32)
        rows, columns = np.floor(32 - xs / TILE).astype(int), np.floor(32 - ys / TILE).astype(int)
        for row in np.unique(rows):
            for column in np.unique(columns):
                file = found.get((continent, row, column))
                if not file or not (minimap / f"{file}.blp").exists():
                    continue
                with Image.open(minimap / f"{file}.blp") as image:
                    texels = np.asarray(image.convert("RGB"), np.float32)
                size = texels.shape[0]
                at_rows, at_columns = np.nonzero(rows == row)[0], np.nonzero(columns == column)[0]
                i = np.clip(((32 - row) * TILE - xs[at_rows]) / TILE * size, 0, size - 1).astype(int)
                j = np.clip(((32 - column) * TILE - ys[at_columns]) / TILE * size, 0, size - 1).astype(int)
                ground[np.ix_(at_rows, at_columns)] = texels[np.ix_(i, j)]
        laid = ground.copy()
        x, y = xs[:, None], ys[None, :]
        drawn = []
        for line in lines:
            for where in line["fields"]["placed"]:
                if where["map"] != continent or abs(where["x"] - middle_x) > reach + 1000 or abs(where["y"] - middle_y) > reach + 1000:
                    continue
                yaw, scale = math.radians(where["yaw"]), where["scale"]
                dx, dy = (where["x"] - x) / scale, (where["y"] - y) / scale
                bx = dx * math.cos(yaw) + dy * math.sin(yaw)    # the building's own x and y of each texel
                by = -dx * math.sin(yaw) + dy * math.cos(yaw)
                for part in sorted(line["fields"]["groups"], key=lambda part: part["low"]):
                    left, bottom, right, top = part["left"], part["bottom"], part["right"], part["top"]
                    u, v = (bx - left) / (right - left), (top - by) / (top - bottom)
                    inside = (u >= 0) & (u < 1) & (v >= 0) & (v < 1)
                    if not inside.any():
                        continue
                    if part["file"] not in cache:
                        with Image.open(OUT / f"{part['file']}.blp") as image:
                            cache[part["file"]] = np.asarray(image.convert("RGBA"), np.float32)
                    texels = cache[part["file"]]
                    th, tw = texels.shape[:2]
                    i = np.clip((v * th).astype(int), 0, th - 1)
                    j = np.clip((u * tw).astype(int), 0, tw - 1)
                    sample = texels[i, j]
                    a = sample[..., 3:4] / 255 * inside[..., None]
                    laid = laid * (1 - a) + sample[..., :3] * a
                drawn.append(where)
        both = np.concatenate([ground, laid], axis=1)
        image = Image.fromarray(np.clip(both, 0, 255).round().astype(np.uint8), "RGB")
        draw = ImageDraw.Draw(image)
        for where in drawn:  # each building's origin, on the right
            i = (north - where["x"]) * TEXELS
            j = (west - where["y"]) * TEXELS + side_texels
            draw.ellipse([j - 2, i - 2, j + 2, i + 2], outline=(255, 0, 255))
        image.save(folder / f"{name}.png")
    print(f"Check pictures: {len(CHECKS)} in {folder}.")


# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
def main():
    args = sys.argv[1:]
    only, processes, checks = None, WALK.PROCESSES, None  # the workers as walk-data's: the app's memory cap
    if "--only" in args:
        at = args.index("--only")
        only = {int(file) for file in args[at + 1].split(",")}
        del args[at:at + 2]
    if "--processes" in args:
        at = args.index("--processes")
        processes = int(args[at + 1])
        del args[at:at + 2]
    if "--check" in args:
        at = args.index("--check")
        checks = (Path(args[at + 1]), Path(args[at + 2]))
        del args[at:at + 3]
    if len(args) != 2:
        print(__doc__.strip().splitlines()[-1], file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    folder, tables = Path(args[0]), Path(args[1])
    game, build = build_of(folder)
    minimaps = folder / "wmo-minimap"
    table = textures(tables)
    areas = area_flags(tables)
    wmos = {}  # [root file] = its WMO ID
    places = WALK.placements(folder)
    by_file = {}
    tilted = []  # the files of the placements left out
    for continent, wheres in places.items():
        for where in wheres:
            if tilt(where["turn"]) > TILT:
                tilted.append(where["file"])
            else:
                by_file.setdefault(where["file"], []).append((continent, where))
    jobs, left_out, sizes = [], {"another shape": 0, "no such part": 0, "nothing drawn": 0, "no part file": 0}, {}
    buildings = {}
    for file in sorted(by_file):
        if only and file not in only:
            continue
        wmo, parts = building(folder / "wmo" / f"{file}.wmo")
        if wmo not in table:
            continue
        buildings[file], wmos[file] = parts, wmo
        for part, blocks in sorted(table[wmo].items()):
            if part >= len(parts):
                left_out["no such part"] += 1
                continue
            for texture in blocks.values():
                if texture not in sizes:
                    sizes[texture] = texture_size(minimaps / f"{texture}.blp")
            if not fits(parts[part][1], blocks, sizes):
                left_out["another shape"] += 1
                continue
            jobs.append((file, part, parts[part][1], blocks, minimaps, folder / "wmo" / f"{file}_{part:03d}.wmo"))
    OUT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    made, total = {}, 0
    with Pool(processes) as pool:
        for done, result in enumerate(pool.imap_unordered(picture, jobs, chunksize=4), 1):
            file, part, rectangle, length = result
            if rectangle:
                made.setdefault(file, {})[part] = rectangle
                total += length
            else:
                left_out[length] += 1
            if done % 250 == 0 or done == len(jobs):
                print(f"{done} of {len(jobs)} pictures made", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
    names = {f"{file}-{part}.blp" for file, parts in made.items() for part in parts}
    for old in OUT.glob("*.blp"):
        if old.name not in names and (not only or int(old.stem.split("-")[0]) in only):
            old.unlink()
    lines = []
    for file in sorted(made):
        groups = []
        for part, (left, bottom, right, top) in sorted(made[file].items()):
            flags, box = buildings[file][part]
            group = {"group": part, "file": f"{file}-{part}", "left": round(left, 2), "bottom": round(bottom, 2),
                     "right": round(right, 2), "top": round(top, 2), "low": round(box[2], 2), "high": round(box[5], 2)}
            if not flags & INDOOR:
                group["outdoor"] = True
            unique = part_id(folder / "wmo" / f"{file}_{part:03d}.wmo")
            if flags & EXTERIOR_LIT and areas.get((wmos[file], unique), 0) & AREA_OUTDOOR:
                group["open"] = True
            groups.append(group)
        wheres = sorted((placed(where, continent) for continent, where in by_file[file]),
                        key=lambda where: (where["map"], where["x"], where["y"]))
        tiles = sorted({key for continent, where in by_file[file] for key in tiles_of(continent, where["box"])})
        lines.append({"set": "Indoors", "key": file, "game": game, "build": build, "src": "game",
                      "fields": {"groups": groups, "placed": wheres, "tiles": tiles}})
    STAGING.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    with open(STAGING, "w", encoding="utf-8") as out:
        for line in lines:
            out.write(json.dumps(line, separators=(",", ":")) + "\n")
    pictures = sum(len(parts) for parts in made.values())
    table_files = {file for file in set(tilted) if building(folder / "wmo" / f"{file}.wmo")[0] in table}
    print(f"Indoor maps: {pictures} pictures of {len(made)} buildings in {OUT.relative_to(ROOT)}, {total / 1e6:.1f} MB; "
          f"left out: {left_out['another shape']} parts whose textures were made for another shape, "
          f"{left_out['no such part']} parts the building lacks, {left_out['nothing drawn']} that draw (almost) nothing, "
          f"{left_out['no part file']} without their part file to check them by, "
          f"{sum(1 for file in tilted if file in table_files)} placements of buildings with indoor maps tilted over {TILT} degrees.")
    print(f"Wrote {STAGING.relative_to(ROOT)}: {len(lines)} buildings, "
          f"{sum(len(line['fields']['placed']) for line in lines)} placements.")
    if checks:
        check(checks[0], checks[1], lines)
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
